    "title": "The Sound at the Door",
    "passage": "Nina heard a soft scratching sound beside the kitchen door. She thought their dog wanted to come inside from the hall. Omar opened the door, but the dog was asleep on a mat farther away. He closed it again, and the scratching returned. Nina stood still and watched the bottom of the door. A loose paper notice hung there, brushing the floor when air moved through the gap. Omar held the paper against the door, and the sound stopped. They moved the notice higher and fixed it with another piece of tape. When they opened and closed the door, nothing scratched. The dog woke up and came over to see them. Nina laughed and said they had answered the paper before the dog. Omar opened the door once more and let the real visitor walk into the kitchen.",
